WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:02.699
Speaker 1: OK, let's jump in to our audience
questions for the week.

00:00:02.699 --> 00:00:07.040
First question is, David, we know Joe Biden
is polling quite well from a standpoint of

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:11.950
approval, but why isn't Kamala Harris nearly
as popular as Joe Biden?

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:13.340
So I didn't even know about this.

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:14.340
I looked into it.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:15.340
And it's true.

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.750
Kamala Harris, his approval rating is quite
a bit lower.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:23.380
Economist YouGov poll has about 51 percent
approval for Joe Biden, only 41 percent approval

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:28.000
for Kamala Harris, lower certainly outside
of the margin of error.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:36.690
In a more recent poll, Harris was at 26, very
favorable with Joe Biden, 33 at very favorable.

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:37.690
There is a gap.

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:39.760
It's not a massive gap.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:44.760
And given that, I don't find it hugely surprising
that Kamala Harris is not polling as well

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.820
as Joe Biden for a few different reasons.

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:50.960
First of all, she was never as popular as
Joe Biden during the primaries.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:56.809
There was a period there, I think, when she
had that bomb drop moment about Biden being

00:00:56.809 --> 00:01:01.629
racist or something during a debate where
she gained a little bit and then she very

00:01:01.629 --> 00:01:05.979
quickly, within a couple of weeks, lost that
and she was never super popular.

00:01:05.979 --> 00:01:11.509
So unless there's some reason why she would
now be very popular, it's not surprising to

00:01:11.509 --> 00:01:15.439
me that she's not doing super well as far
as approval.

00:01:15.439 --> 00:01:21.270
The second piece of it is Joe Biden often
talks about the Biden Harris administration

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:24.119
and Kamala Harris is often there at different
things.

00:01:24.119 --> 00:01:30.639
But she's not been particularly present as
a major player in a lot of the things that

00:01:30.639 --> 00:01:32.880
are what makes Joe Biden popular today.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:35.039
I'm not saying she wasn't a major player.

00:01:35.039 --> 00:01:39.310
I'm saying it just hasn't been apparent from
much of the way that the stories have been

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:40.310
covered.

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:45.569
Covid stimulus, for example, it really was
framed as this is Biden negotiating and then

00:01:45.569 --> 00:01:47.310
Democrats in the House and Senate getting
it done.

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:53.959
And Harris is there in the room, as has often
been said, but she's not sufficiently connected

00:01:53.959 --> 00:01:54.959
to it.

00:01:54.959 --> 00:02:00.779
And then lastly, there is a kind of personality
aspect, which is, as the vice president, she

00:02:00.779 --> 00:02:02.649
hasn't taken the spotlight.

00:02:02.649 --> 00:02:05.309
Now, some may say, well, she's not been allowed
to.

00:02:05.309 --> 00:02:07.759
That may be I'm not saying that she's chosen
not to.

00:02:07.759 --> 00:02:10.750
I'm saying she hasn't been in the spotlight.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:16.680
And that means that the discourse is sort
of happening around her more than being shaped

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:18.780
by her actions herself.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:23.010
Now, there's one last thing on, and it's sort
of a propagandistic thing.

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:26.250
We've talked about how
Speaker 4: the

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:33.900
Speaker 1: Republican Party and right wing
media and others have concocted the immigration

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:36.030
crisis, the crisis at the border.

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:40.069
Now, the truth is things aren't much different
at the border than they were under Donald

00:02:40.069 --> 00:02:41.489
Trump.

00:02:41.489 --> 00:02:44.450
They've gotten significantly better actually
in the last six weeks, which we've reported

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:45.450
on.

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:49.420
But the the narrative has been it's a border
crisis.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:54.110
And it worked in that back in June, only 28
percent of the country thought there was a

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:56.879
crisis at the border last month.

00:02:56.879 --> 00:02:59.890
Forty eight percent of the country believe
there was a crisis at the border.

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:01.249
So the propaganda has worked.

00:03:01.249 --> 00:03:02.909
How does this relate to Comilla?

00:03:02.909 --> 00:03:09.480
It relates to Kamala Harris because she was
designated as the person who was going to

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:12.209
handle the situation at the border.

00:03:12.209 --> 00:03:17.160
Now, if you believe it's a crisis and you
believe what Fox News says, that nothing's

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:22.790
been done and you remember that it was assigned
to Kamala Harris, you probably don't have

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:27.560
a particularly high view of favorable view
of Kamala Harris.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:32.209
So I think that the negativity around that
probably is not is not helping her either.

00:03:32.209 --> 00:03:33.639
That's my sense.

00:03:33.639 --> 00:03:36.010
Never really popular to begin with.

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:38.829
Not in the spotlight for Joe Biden's successes.

00:03:38.829 --> 00:03:44.180
And I don't want to say thrown under the bus,
but tied to.

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:50.970
A fabricated so-called crisis at the border
because it was assigned to her portfolio and

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:55.530
the right wing media narrative is just that
the crisis continues regardless of what the

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:56.620
truth is there.

00:03:56.620 --> 00:04:00.730
Send me your thoughts if you have a different
view as to why Carmella's approval is lower

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:01.799
than than Biden's.

00:04:01.799 --> 00:04:06.769
And last thing, I think generally the vice
president has a lower approval than the president.

00:04:06.769 --> 00:04:10.090
I think it was the case with Mike Pence and
Donald Trump for most of his presidency.

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:11.090
Correct me if I'm wrong.

00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:12.920
I'm going from memory.

00:04:12.920 --> 00:06:02.520
It doesn't strike me as shocking for that
reason either.

